WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:00.630 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  another day and another rally with  thousands of angry people taking to the  streets in sri lanka  they came from around the country  desperate to be heard  people are facing hardships even those  who have money don't have goods to buy  children students parents everyone is  facing problems  after 25 years abroad i started farming  i don't have fertilizer my child doesn't  have milk powder in the same way every  sector is affected everyone understands  this  the rally in nuger on the outskirts of  the capital colombo was organized by the  national people power coalition  its leaders say the mainstream political  parties are responsible for the current  state of affairs and are calling for  political change the crowds carried  banners that said 74 years of corruption  enough is enough  people are crying patients are dying and  the government is lying  i want the government to get a clear  message that the people have had enough  and it is time that they allow the  people to make a new choice and form a  new government that can at least start  to resolve some of these issues that's  going to be a daunting task for anyone  who dares the country's foreign reserves  have hit rock bottom with no money for  imports of vital food medicines cooking  gas and fuel which are increasing in  price globally as well as in sri lanka  people are angry at having to spend  hours in queues for essential items  i've not eaten from morning i can't go  to work the pay we get is not increasing  but they have increased prices of all  food items  and they say sri lanka is not the only  country facing economic trouble at  present but they point out that  mismanagement bad planning and  corruption has aggravated things  on wednesday president gotabe rajpaksa  hosted an all-party conference telling  participants they must unite to find  solutions to the current situation but a  number of those gathered here in nugeda  told al jazeera that the president's  words come too late to be taken  seriously  the national people's power is the  latest political front to organize  demonstrations like this against  economic  hardships widespread anger desperation  and frustration has brought thousands of  peoples onto the street  minerva fernandez al jazeera nuger

